msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_1"
msgstr "{{@ class $titleClass}}It's craftier than anything we've come up against. And it has one trick that there's still no way to counter.{{/}}\n\nDamn it! Why are things never easy? Plan A failed. It was beautiful, spectacular, but it failed.\n\nEveryone thought the {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Marduk{{/}} was our ace in the hole. A huge flying ship with guns bigger than the Dora's cannon.\n\nOne salvo, and all our problems would be solved. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}The Dark Tower{{/}} destroyed; the Nazis, or what was left of them, neutralized. And all those thousands of tanks that they'd prepared for attack back in the '40s would stay here to rust forever.\n\nBut I forgot rule number one: in the anomaly, things are never easy. The shells got stuck in that damned shield. And to take it out, we'd need to destroy the thing that generates it.\n\nBut that {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Spider{{/}} is craftier than anything we've come up against. First you need to get to it. And then, when all that's left is to deliver the final blow, it activates the damned Magnus and retreats to its lair to lick its wounds. And hurls us a few phases back.\n\nAlright, enough waxing lyrical. It's time for action. Either we deactivate that shield and blow the Tower to hell, or we'll stay here forever.\n\nThe command built its huge ship, even gave it the name of a god and thought the problem was solved. But in the end, here we are again. Gods fail us. Tanks don't.\n\n{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n{{@ class $textManual}}\"Use the tactical map and coordinate your actions. Mark the point you are heading to so that the platoon moves with you. Or proceed to a position chosen by another commander. Always stick together.\"{{/}}"

